And he said, I think I have a great opportunity for you.

24
00:02:16,960 --> 00:02:24,800
And it turned out to be just that because Sean really introduced me to this idea of this test learned approach where experimentation drives growth.

25
00:02:24,960 --> 00:02:36,320
So at the time, we were doing a lot of paid marketing and the specific role was around testing creative, which at the time was these 468 by 60 banners.

26
00:02:36,720 --> 00:02:37,920
So we had a lot of fun with that.

27
00:02:39,120 --> 00:02:41,280
And we can we have some great stories from that.

28
00:02:41,520 --> 00:02:49,520
But yeah, and I think Sean and I really very quickly realized that we had a sort of a shared passion and curiosity around growth.

29
00:02:50,160 --> 00:02:55,680
And so even after uproar dot com, Sean went in some different directions.

30
00:02:55,840 --> 00:03:05,200
I went in some different directions, both entrepreneurial and both really trying to understand and learn growth, but we always stayed in touch and formed a really nice friendship along the way, I think.

31
00:03:05,440 --> 00:03:10,400
I mean, I guess Sean will have to confirm that, mostly because we both sail, so it gives us something to talk about.

32
00:03:11,760 --> 00:03:18,880
But then as I was moving on from Teltek and Robokiller, Sean had started this podcast, the Breakout Growth Podcast.

33
00:03:19,280 --> 00:03:26,880
And I think I was his first recording, though not his first guest, but I was giving him some thoughts in the background and helping him with a few things.

34
00:03:27,040 --> 00:03:28,400
We wrote some growth studies together.

35
00:03:29,040 --> 00:03:34,640
And eventually it just led to us, Sean, I think Sean just got tired and I broke him down and he said, Okay, fine.

36
00:03:35,440 --> 00:03:36,400
You can be my cohost.

37
